      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T15:50:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh this is a `PrintWriter`. It can be configured to auto-flush or not, so we can\u0027t assume it would flush. But the errors at the start of the function (`getErrPrintWriter().println`) also have this problem and they *definitely* don\u0027t flush. Let me fix all of them in a follow-on patch?",
